! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1260's CONSTANTS AND INTERRUPT TABLE --
! PDF p.86 (printed p.83), octal 023042.00-023070.00, transcribed
! VERBATIM at the listing's own addresses and checked bit-exactly by
! verify_ax5b_160k_listing.py.
!
! WHY THIS BLOCK.  It is the harness the p.71 comparison driver needs
! (ax5b_160105_compare.strap), and it SETTLES THREE THINGS that
! earlier transcriptions in this project had to leave open or infer.
!
! 1. 160K7 IS THE ILLEGAL OP.  ax5b_16082_op_ad.strap SYN'd 160K7 from
!    "LX,$X4,160K7 -> 23050.10 10" on p.41 and its header said, under
!    "NOT TRACED": "WHAT 160K7 CONTAINS.  Only its address, 023050.00,
!    is printed here.  The block's SHAPE ... reads like self-modifying
!    code planting an invalid operation code ... Nothing on these pages
!    says so."  p.86 says so:
!        160K7  %8@DD%BU,32,8@,3740   -ILLEGAL OP, NO. 31.
!    The inference was right and is now a printed fact.
!
! 2. 160K16 IS "BD,16086A", confirming the external
!    ax5b_16086_ds.strap SYN'd from p.43's "LX,$X4,160K16".
!
! 3. THE INTERRUPT TABLE IS 64 WORDS, STATED RATHER THAN REASONED.
!        160IT   DR%BU,64,8@,64    023201.00
!        160DMP  XW,0,0,0,0        023301.00
!    023301 - 023201 = 0o100 = 64.  run_tests.sh's "The interruption
!    mechanism" section had REASONED the units were "64 full words,
!    from 160IT at 023201.00 to 160DMP at 023301.00"; the DR row
!    states the 64 directly.
!
! AND 160K12 IS THE TABLE'S DEFAULT ENTRY: "BD,16010A" twice, so every
! interruption disables and branches to the label p.71 calls "-ALL
! INTRPTS EXCEPT AD ENTER HERE."  160XW1 ("XW,0,64,160IT" -- count 64,
! refill 160IT) is what the comparison driver's CB+ loop walks to copy
! it into all 64 slots.
!
! IT ALSO EXPOSED AN ASSEMBLER GAP, the third this routine has found.
! "C+I,$X1,160DMP" at 023044.00 prints "23301.03 00" -- 160DMP's WORD
! address in bits 0-17 -- and the assembler evaluated the label to a
! BIT address and wrapped it.  Count-type immediates now use
! eval_addr_field with shift 6, exactly as XW's refill field already
! did: a label scales >>6, a bare integer counts words, so
! "LCI,$X1,18" is unchanged.  (The first two gaps: TRANSMIT/SWAP not
! encodable at all, found by p.45's TI; XW's fourth operand masked to
! one bit, found by 160S1's single XW row.)
!
! ENCODING ONLY: these are constants, with nothing to execute.  The
! rows past 023070.00 -- 160XW5-9, USAWD, USALVE, 160INT, 160IT,
! 160DMP, BOUND0, BOUND1 -- are not transcribed here; USALVE needs
! LVE and the DR reserves are better given to whatever program
! actually runs the table.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS: one.  Numeric labels prefixed "L".  Every external is
! given by SYN at the address this block's own rows print for it.

L160DMP SYN, (8)23301.0
L16035  SYN, (8)14642.0
L16090  SYN, (8)21512.40
L16097  SYN, (8)22072.0
L16010A SYN, (8)22371.40
L16086A SYN, (8)21372.40
L160107 SYN, (8)22372.0
L160IT  SYN, (8)23201.0
        SLC, (8)23042.0
L160K1  XW, (8)777777.60, 0, 0
L160K2  SX, $X1, L160DMP
        NOP
L160K3  C+I, $X1, L160DMP
        NOP
L160K4  SV, $X1, L160DMP
        NOP
L160K5  BD, L16035
        BD, L16035
L160K6  BD, L16090
        NOP
L160K7  DD(BU,32,8), (8)3740     ! -ILLEGAL OP, NO. 31.
        NOP
L160K8  BD, L16097
        NOP
L160K9  XW, -1.0, 0, 0
L160K10 XW, 1.0, 1, 0
L160K11 XW, -3.0, 63, 0
L160K12 BD, L16010A
        BD, L16010A
L160K13 NOP
        NOP
L160K14 XW, -0.1, 0, 0
L160K15 XW, -(8)777777.60, 0, 0
L160K16 BD, L16086A
        BD, L16086A
L160K17 BD, L160107
        BD, L160107
L160AD1 NOP
L160AD2 NOP
L160AD3 NOP
        NOP
L160XW1 XW, 0, 64, L160IT
L160XW2 XW, 0, 48, 0
L160XW3 XW, (8)101.0, 0, 0
L160XW4 XW, 0, 63, L160IT
        END, L160K1
